From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the guest stops drawing while the window cannot be seen

What: with OmacVM.app's "Pause drawing while hidden" on (the app's defaults
key pauseWhileHidden, watched live; OMACVM_GUEST_PAUSE=1 or 0 decides
instead), the guest's display agent is told {"unseen": ["Virtual-1"]} over
org.omacvm.display once the main window has been out of sight for 2 s:
macOS's occlusion says none of it is on screen (minimised, wholly covered,
on a Space not shown, closed with Keep running), or the screen is locked,
the displays sleep or another user is on the console. The agent turns that
output's display off (DPMS). Seen again: {"unseen": []} at once; until the
guest's first frame the window keeps its last picture, not QEMU's "display
not active" one. Only an agent that says "pause": 1 in its hello is told (a
restarted agent again at its hello). The channel drops a line it cannot
write at once, so "unseen" is a lease said again every 5 s (the agent turns
its displays on after 15 s without it) and "seen" is said again every 0.25 s
until the guest's first frame (at most 5 s). qemu.log: the switch at start
and on a change; each word for the guest and whether it got it (sent, or why
not: the channel closed, no hello yet, an agent that cannot pause, a line
the channel did not take), only when that changes and at most 20 lines in 10
minutes, so the lease and the repeated "seen" add none; a window out of
sight for 2 s with nobody to tell, once; after each pause how long it was
and when the guest's first two frames came after the window was seen.
OMACVM_PRESENT_HIDDEN=1 keeps the guest drawing too.

Why: omacvm-cocoa-present-unseen.patch stops QEMU's copy for an unseen
window, but the guest kept drawing every frame at the display's rate:
Hyprland, the apps, virgl on the Mac's GPU (M1 Max, a video in the hidden
test VM: 13.9 W against 17.4 W visible, macOS idle 3.9 W). A macOS app
gets no frames for a window nobody sees. With the guest's display off
there are no vblanks, so Wayland apps stop drawing too; sound, downloads,
timers and the guest's own work go on. Visible windows are not touched.
The log of the words: on 2026-11-07 a VM out of sight for 20 minutes never
paused and neither QEMU nor the guest said why (a word dropped, a share, a
DPMS request that failed).

Upstream: not sent (OmacVM's display channel).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-guest-pause.sh (the rules, and the
wiring in the patched ui/cocoa.m at build time); src/app/guest/tests/
test_omacvm_displays.py (the agent's side). Applies after
omacvm-cocoa-present-unseen.patch and omacvm-cocoa-present-damage.patch.

